        <dialog class="about-dialog" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
          <div class="card-body">
            <button class="icon-btn card-close" type="button" aria-label="Close" data-close-about autofocus><svg class="close" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 6 12 12M18 6 6 18"/></svg></button>
            <div class="card-side">
              <figure class="card-portrait">
                <picture>
                  <source type="image/webp" srcset="assets/media/profile-480.webp 480w, assets/media/profile-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 720px) 96px, 272px" />
                  <img src="assets/media/profile-960.webp" width="960" height="995" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Akhil Theerthala" />
                </picture>
                <figcaption>Bengaluru, India</figcaption>
              </figure>
              <dl class="card-now">
                <div><dt>Now</dt><dd>Calibrated LLM safeguards and agentic workflows for consumer-finance market intelligence at Perfios.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Reading</dt><dd>Interpretability and evaluation of LLMs and agentic systems.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Research</dt><dd>Training-data attribution, with Georgia Tech&#39;s HCAI Lab.</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Studying</dt><dd>MS in Data Science, IIIT Hyderabad.</dd></div>
              </dl>
            </div>
            <div class="card-main">
              <div class="card-head">
                <p class="kicker">About</p>
                <h2 id="about-title">Akhil Theerthala</h2>
                <p class="card-role">Senior Member Data Scientist, Perfios Software Solutions · Bengaluru, India</p>
              </div>
              <div class="card-text">
                <p>I am a Senior Member Data Scientist at Perfios Software Solutions in Bengaluru. I also build document-AI systems for banks, lenders, and insurers, such as document classifiers, table detection, and VLMs adapted to dense financial documents.</p>
                <p>My research is on data curation and LLM evaluation. I build synthetic training data, such as personal-finance data grounded in behavioral finance. I also work on benchmarks for financial agents and on steering for language models. I look for methods that still work under real limits on latency, cost, and auditability.</p>
              </div>
              <h3 class="card-sub">Research interests</h3>
              <ul class="card-interests">
                <li>Data curation for reliable models</li>
                <li>Financial AI and agentic systems</li>
                <li>Document AI and VLM adaptation</li>
                <li>LLM evaluation and interpretability</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="card-actions">
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:akhiltvsn@gmail.com">Email me</a>
                <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/Akhil-Theerthala" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
                <a class="btn" href="https://huggingface.co/Akhil-Theerthala" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Hugging Face<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
                <a class="btn" href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=_H1O3ScAAAAJ&amp;hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Google Scholar<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
                <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/akhil-theerthala/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
                <a class="btn" href="https://x.com/thesilvervein" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">X<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </dialog>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="cv">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head reveal"><h2>Experience</h2></div>
          <ol class="timeline">
          <li class="role reveal current">
            <time>Apr 2025 - Present</time>
            <div>
              <h3>Senior Member Data Scientist <span>Perfios Software Solutions</span></h3>
              <ul>
              <li>Leading uncertainty-quantification research for financial LLMs. I am building a BFSI-specific benchmark to audit cultural and demographic bias and to measure calibration under different levels of numerical precision. I also probe the cues behind miscalibration and test steering, context conditioning, and fine-tuning as mitigations.</li>
              <li>Developing guardrails for LLM and agent applications in banking. I map where these applications are vulnerable and build adversarial and failure-mode evaluations. I also test output controls against the Reserve Bank of India&#39;s FREE-AI recommendations for safe, fair, explainable, and robust AI.</li>
              <li>Built an agentic market-intelligence workflow for consumer banking products. It analyzes customer needs and competitive positioning to find gaps in the product line.</li>
              <li>Developed and now monitor a reference-free document image-quality service built on ViT regression. In production, it flags low-quality documents at <strong>92% precision</strong> before they reach HDB&#39;s downstream applications.</li>
              <li>Adapted PaliGemma2 with LoRA for financial documents and reached a <strong>0.85 TEDS</strong> score on internal benchmarks for structured document understanding.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="role reveal current">
            <time>Aug 2025 - Present</time>
            <div>
              <h3>Research Volunteer <span>FSIL &amp; HCAI Labs, Georgia Tech</span></h3>
              <ul>
              <li>Co-authored FinForge, a pipeline that generates semi-synthetic benchmarks for financial tasks. The paper was accepted at the AAAI 2026 Workshop on Agentic AI in Financial Services.</li>
              <li>Contributed to the Role Steering of Language Models for Social Simulations paper at the COLM 2026 Social Simulations Workshop. I also contributed to the Data Attribution Should Guide Pretraining paper at the NeurIPS 2026 ATTRIB Workshop.</li>
              <li>Contributing to Capabilibarav2, an HCAI Lab project on training-data attribution that traces which source documents influence a language model&#39;s outputs.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="role reveal">
            <time>Jun 2023 - Apr 2025</time>
            <div>
              <h3>Member Data Scientist <span>Perfios Software Solutions</span></h3>
              <ul>
              <li>Distilled and quantized a multimodal document classifier into a small student model. Latency fell from <strong>8s to 200ms</strong> with F1 unchanged in production-scale evaluation.</li>
              <li>Improved generalized table detection accuracy by <strong>27.6%</strong> with semi-synthetic data curation and a systematic study of YOLOv8 variants. The gain carried through to the downstream table-structure recognition (TSR) module.</li>
              <li>Integrated a semantic row-detection module, built on fine-tuned text encoders, into the production TSR pipeline. It adds <strong>under 40ms</strong> of turnaround time and keeps throughput unchanged.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </li>
          </ol>
          
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section band" id="work">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head reveal"><h2>Projects</h2></div>
          <div class="projects">
        <article class="project reveal" id="project-localxiv" style="--i:0">
          <div class="project-media">
          <figure class="cover">
            <img src="assets/media/localxiv-cover.webp" width="1920" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="LocalXiv on macOS: Attention Is All You Need open in the dark reader with its contents sidebar, and the paper's Overview figure in a second window." />
          </figure>
          </div>
          <div class="project-text">
            <p class="kicker project-kicker"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Open source · Mac app · Sep 2026</p>
            <h3>LocalXiv</h3>
