        <article class="project reveal" id="project-crowdfunding-social-signals" style="--i:0">
          <div class="project-media">
          <figure class="drivers">
            <figcaption><b>What the original models ranked</b><span>Permutation importance, scaled so the top feature in each panel is 1. Effects come from the partial-dependence plots.</span></figcaption>
            <div class="drivers-panels">
              <section class="drivers-panel">
                <p class="drivers-title">Engagement on a Facebook post</p>
                <p class="drivers-meta">8,786 posts from the GoFundMe, Indiegogo and Kickstarter pages</p>
                <ol class="drivers-bars" aria-label="Engagement on a Facebook post">
                  <li class="flagged" style="--v:1">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Post views<sup>1</sup></span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">Strong rise</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">1.00</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.51">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Page that posted it</span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">GoFundMe highest</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.51</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.08">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Page likes at posting</span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">Small rise</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.08</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.08">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Post age</span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">More likes, fewer comments</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.08</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.06">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Video post</span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">Lower than links</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.06</span>
                  </li>
                  <li class="flagged" style="--v:0.02">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Names a person<sup>3</sup></span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">Flat</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.02</span>
                  </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="drivers-foot">No text feature stands out: all 38, from topics and emotions to readability, score 0.02 or less.</p>
              </section>
              <section class="drivers-panel">
                <p class="drivers-title">Kickstarter campaign success</p>
                <p class="drivers-meta">549 of the 1,023 campaigns Kickstarter promoted, 54 of which failed</p>
                <ol class="drivers-bars has-noise" aria-label="Kickstarter campaign success" style="--noise:0.29">
                  <li class="flagged" style="--v:1">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Projects the creator backed<sup>2</sup></span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">Rises, then levels</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">1.00</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.52">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Shares of the post</span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">Peaks near 15</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.52</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.47">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Launch month</span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">October to December lower</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.47</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.43">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Runs 2 weeks to 1 month</span>
                      
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.43</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.38">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Individual creator, not a team</span>
                      
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.38</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.34">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Comments on the post</span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">Mixed</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.34</span>
                  </li>
                  <li style="--v:0.32">
                    <span class="drivers-row">
                      <span class="drivers-label">Likes on the post</span>
                      <span class="drivers-effect">Peaks near 50</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="drivers-track" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
                    <span class="drivers-value">0.32</span>
                  </li>
                </ol>
                <p class="drivers-foot">The notebook kept only campaigns its region map called North American, which left out Canada and nine US states. It then dropped the 80 campaigns that raised 10 times their goal or more, all of which had succeeded.</p>
              </section>
            </div>
            <ul class="drivers-notes">
              <li><b>1</b><span>Leak: post views is the largest of the post&#39;s view, reaction, comment and share counts, so it contains what the model predicts.</span></li>
              <li><b>2</b><span>Timing: backing counts were read from creator profiles after the campaigns ended, so they can include later backing.</span></li>
              <li><b>3</b><span>Text: zeros in the topic and emotion scores were replaced with small random values, entities were found in lowercased text, and the topic vocabulary was fitted on all posts before the split. With post views in the model, low text scores do not show that text is uninformative.</span></li>
              <li><i class="swatch" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Noise: shuffling one feature raised accuracy by 0.29 on this scale, so the faded start of each success bar is within noise. The success scores come from 110 campaigns: 11 failed, and 27 were also in the training data.</span></li>
              <li><b></b><span>The engagement scores compare log-scale predictions with raw counts, so the few posts with the largest counts drive them. Neither the bar sizes nor their order is exact.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </figure>
          </div>
          <div class="project-text">
            <p class="kicker project-kicker"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Research · B.Tech project · Mar 2024</p>
            <h3>Social Media Signals and Crowdfunding Success</h3>
            <p class="project-desc">My B.Tech research, which I extended after graduating, asked what drives engagement with crowdfunding posts on Facebook, and whether that engagement predicts a campaign&#39;s success. In the two models shown, the top feature can leak the outcome, and the text features were built with defects, so their low scores say little about text. A 2026 re-audit retired those methods, and I am rebuilding the study on archived Kickstarter pages.</p>
            
            <div class="project-links">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/Akhil-Theerthala/Crowdfunding-Social-Media-Drivers" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub<span class="sr-only">: Social Media Signals and Crowdfunding Success</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
