          <li class="pub reveal" id="paper-finforge-semi-synthetic-financial-benchmark-generation" style="--i:2">
            <div class="pub-thumb"><img src="assets/media/paper-finforge.webp" width="960" height="1242" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="First page of FinForge: Semi-Synthetic Financial Benchmark Generation" /></div>
            <div>
              <p class="pub-venue"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>Agentic AI in Financial Services Workshop, AAAI 2026<span class="pub-role">Major contribution</span></p>
              <h3><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.06747" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">FinForge: Semi-Synthetic Financial Benchmark Generation<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></h3>
              <p class="pub-authors">Glenn Matlin, <strong>Akhil Theerthala</strong>, Anant Gupta, Anirudh JM, Rayan Castilla, Yi Mei Ng, Sudheer Chava</p>
              <details><summary>Abstract</summary><p>A scalable semi-synthetic pipeline for building finance-specific LM benchmarks from authoritative sources using expert-guided curation and controlled LM synthesis. FinForge-5k contains 5,000+ human-validated question-answer pairs across 11 finance subdomains and reveals substantial gaps in financial reasoning, even as leading models approach 80% accuracy.</p></details>
              <ul class="tags" aria-label="Topics"><li>Benchmarks</li><li>Agentic AI</li><li>Finance</li></ul>
              <div class="pub-actions"><a class="btn btn-small btn-primary" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.06747" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">arXiv<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a><button class="btn btn-small copy-btn" type="button" data-copy="@misc{matlin2026finforge,
